_12.raw\n20241018_FU_05_13.raw\n20241018_FU_05_15.raw\n20241018_FU_05_16.raw\n20241018_FU_05_17.raw\n20241018_FU_05_19.raw\n20241018_FU_05_20.raw\n20241018_FU_05_21.raw\n\nPublication text and PRIDE metadata:\n[TITLE]\nIdentification of TDP-43 - TAU interactions by XL-MS\n\n[ABSTRACT]\nIdentification of TDP-43 - TAU interactions by XL-MS (DSS). The interactions were identified in for equimolar amount of TDP-43 - TAU and, as control, TDP-43 and MBP. After 30 minutes from the induction of phase separation, samples were either analyzed (bulk condition) or subjected to centrifugation (10min at 21’000g) to pellet the formed condensates.\n\n[METHODS]\nFor XL-MS analysis, three independent experiments were conducted to determine whether TDP-43 can physically interact with TAU and to characterize the topology of this interaction. 10\u202fµM TDP-43-TEV-MBP-His₆ was cleaved with 0.08\u202fmg/ml His₆-TEV protease in the presence of either 10\u202fµM MBP (control) or 10\u202fµM TAU441 in 50\u202fµl of reaction buffer (20\u202fmM HEPES, 150\u202fmM NaCl, 1\u202fmM DTT, pH 7.5). After 30 minutes from the induction of phase separation, samples were either analyzed (bulk condition) or subjected to centrifugation (10min at 21’000g) to pellet the formed condensates. For the pellet condition, the resulting pellet was resuspended in 50µl reaction buffer. Both bulk and pellet samples from TDP-43 incubated with MBP or TAU were subjected to crosslinking reaction with 1mM isotope labeled di-succimidylsuberate (DSS-d0 and DSS-d12, Creative Molecules Inc.). After 5 minutes of reaction, the samples were subjected to liquid nitrogen quenching and thawed in 50mM Ammonium bicarbonate. Upon quenching, samples were dried, dissolved in 8\u2009M Urea, reduced (5\u2009mM TCEP), and alkylated (10\u2009mM iodoacetamide). The proteolysis was performed overnight at 37\u2009°C in 1\u2009M urea with 1µg trypsin (Promega, Sequencing grade). After quenching (5% formic acid) peptides were subjected to cleanup according to manufacture procedures (AttractSPE Tips, Affinisep). Data acquisition: Liquid chromatography-tandem mass spectrometry (LC-MS/MS) measurements were performed on Orbitrap QExactive+ MS coupled to a Dionex Ultimate 3000 RSLCnano System liquid chromatography system. Peptides were loaded on a commercial trap column (μ-Precolumn C18 PepMap100, C18, 300\u2009μm I.D., 5\u2009μm particle size) and separated using a reverse phase column Thermo PepMap100 C18 (50\u2009cm length, 75\u2009μm inner diameter, 35\u2009μm particle size). For the identification of crosslinking peptides in DDA mode, an LC method was set up to separate peptides across a gradient from 8%B to 25%B in 60 min and from 25%B to 50%B in 4\u2009min (buffer A: 0.1% (v/v) formic acid; buffer B: 0.1% (v/v) formic acid, 80% (v/v) acetonitrile). The acquisition method was performed with one MS1 scan followed by a maximum of 20 scans for the top 20 most intense peptides (TOP20) with MS1 scans (R\u2009=\u200970,000 at 400\u2009m/z, maxIT\u2009=\u2009100\u2009ms AGC=3e6), HCD fragmentation (NCE\u2009=\u200930%), isolation windows (1.6m/z) and MS2 scans (R\u2009=\u200917,500 at 400\u2009m/z, maxIT\u2009=\u200950\u2009ms, AGC\u2009=\u20091e5). A dynamic exclusion of 30\u2009s was applied, and charge states lower than three and higher than seven were rejected for the isolation.\n\n\nPreviously extracted organism(s) and NCBI taxid(s):\nHomo sapiens (human)\n\n---\n\nTASKS\n\n1. Identify the distinct biological/experimental conditions described by the publication, PRIDE metadata, and filenames.\n\n2. Assign every raw file to exactly one cluster.\n\n3. Define clusters using the smallest number of biologically meaningful groups. Do not over-cluster based only on replicate, fraction, or run-number differences.\n\n4. For each cluster, report:\n   - cluster_id: "cluster_1", "cluster_2", etc.\n   - cluster_label: short machine-readable label using lowercase words separated by underscores\n   - description: concise human-readable summary of the condition\n   - organism: full scientific name of the proteome/sample organism\n   - taxid: NCBI Taxonomy CURIE, e.g. "NCBITaxon:9606"; use null if unknown\n   - crosslinker: crosslinking reagent; use null if unknown\n   - biological_condition: short phrase describing the treatment/control/state\n   - files: list of raw filenames assigned to this cluster\n   - confidence: "high", "medium", or "low"\n   - evidence_quote: exact sentence or short phrase from the publication, PRIDE metadata, or filename pattern that supports this cluster assignment\n   - reasoning: brief explanation of why these files belong together\n\n5. Assign files that cannot be confidently interpreted to cluster_0 with:\n   - cluster_label: "unassigned"\n   - confidence: "low"\n   - evidence_quote: null\n   - reasoning: explain why assignment was not possible\n\n6. QC, calibrant, blank, wash, or test files should be assigned to cluster_0 unless the publication clearly states they are part of the biological experiment.\n\n7. If all biological files appear to come from one condition, create only cluster_1 plus cluster_0 if there are unassigned/QC files.\n\n8. Confidence guidelines:\n   - "high": filenames and publication/metadata agree clearly\n   - "medium": assignment is likely but partially inferred from filenames or incomplete metadata\n   - "low": weak evidence, ambiguous naming, missing metadata, or conflicting information\n\n9. If publication text and filenames conflict, prioritize the publication/PRIDE metadata, but mention the conflict in reasoning.\n\n10. Return ONLY valid JSON. Do not include markdown, comments, or explanatory text outside the JSON.\n\n---\n\nOUTPUT JSON STRUCTURE\n\n{\n  "clusters": [\n    {\n      "cluster_id": "cluster_1",\n      "cluster_label": "yeast_glucose_bs3",\n      "description": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae samples grown in glucose-rich medium and crosslinked with BS3.",\n      "organism": "Saccharomyces cerevisiae",\n      "taxid": "NCBITaxon:4932",\n      "crosslinker": "BS3",\n      "biological_condition": "glucose-rich medium",\n      "files": [\n        "YeastGlu_R1.raw",\n        "YeastGlu_R2.raw",\n        "YeastGlu_fraction_01.raw"\n      ],\n      "confidence": "high",\n      "evidence_quote": "Yeast cells were cultured in glucose- or glycerol-containing medium and crosslinked with BS3.",\n      "reasoning": "The filenames contain Glu and the publication states that glucose-grown yeast samples were crosslinked with BS3."\n    },\n    {\n      "cluster_id": "cluster_0",\n      "cluster_label": "unassigned",\n      "description": "Files that could not be confidently assigned to a biological XL-MS condition.",\n      "organism": null,\n      "taxid": null,\n      "crosslinker": null,\n      "biological_condition": null,\n      "files": [\n        "calibrant.raw",\n        "QC.raw"\n      ],\n      "confidence": "low",\n      "evidence_quote": null,\n      "reasoning": "These files appear to be QC or calibration runs rather than biological samples."\n    }\n  ],\n  "summary": {\n    "n_input_files": 5,\n    "n_assigned_files": 3,\n    "n_unassigned_files": 2,\n    "n_biological_clusters": 1,\n    "overall_confidence": "high"\n  }\n}'}], 'model': 'gpt-5.4-nano-2026-03-17', 'store': True, 'temperature': 0.3}}
